text:
sre-bot: :rotating_light: PAGER - INC-2026-17 - api-gateway 'generate' route elevated errors and latency. p95=2300ms, 5xx=8%, spike correlated with api-key acme-labs-prod. Link: https://redwood/incident/INC-2026-17

maya: I'm oncall. Acknowledging. Gathering context now — @oli can you confirm if this is traffic-pattern or backend regression? @jordan we may need immediate SDK guidance for retry behavior for affected customers.

oli: Looking at traces — large burst of concurrent streaming requests from that key, many with long-lived connections. Not seeing an obvious NPE in model infra. Likely load-induced timeouts causing retries and amplification. Plan (short): 1) Apply per-key rate limit to throttle the surge, 2) disable streaming for that key, 3) temporarily cap max seq length for requests from the key. Executing now.

oli: Executing mitigation commands: 
```bash
# limit to 50 rps for the key
redwoodctl edge-ratelimit set --key acme-labs-prod --rps 50
# disable streaming chunks for that subject
redwoodctl feature-flag set --feature streaming --subject acme-labs-prod --state off
# reduce model max tokens for that key
redwoodctl route-config update --route generate --subject acme-labs-prod --max-tokens 1024
```

sre-bot: ACTION - edge-ratelimit applied for acme-labs-prod, feature-flag streaming toggled, route config updated (operator: oli).

maya: Good. Start a brief monitoring window. @sam please pull list of customers impacted and prepare comms if it's customer-facing. Jordan, once we have a stable mitigation, we need a short SDK advisory for clients: adjust retry/backoff and idempotency guidance.

jordan: Draft guidance below — short and prescriptive so customers can apply without code churn. Key points: - Treat 429 and 5xx as retryable only for idempotent operations. - Reduce client max retries to 3 during the incident window. - Use jittered exponential backoff (full jitter). - Always require Idempotency-Key header for non-idempotent POSTs that may be retried by clients. Example JS pattern: 
```js
// minimal backoff + idempotency example
const DEFAULT_RETRIES = 3;
const shouldRetry = (err) => err.status === 429 || (err.status >= 500 && err.status < 600);
async function callWithBackoff(fn, retries = DEFAULT_RETRIES) {
  for (let i = 0; i <= retries; i++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (err) {
      if (!shouldRetry(err)) throw err;
      if (i === retries) throw err;
      const base = Math.min(1000 * 2 ** i, 10000);
      const backoff = Math.random() * base; // full jitter
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
    }
  }
}

// when issuing non-idempotent requests ensure header:
// "Idempotency-Key": "<uuid>"
```

jordan: Also recommend clients detect streaming-disabled responses (HTTP 422 with body {"reason":"streaming_disabled_for_key"}) and fall back to non-streaming path rather than aggressive retries. SDK patch ready to toggle defaults: reduce retries -> 3, enable jitter=true, and surface errors with clear advice.

sam: Support note: impacted customers list pulled — Acme Labs (acme-labs-prod) primary, 2 dev orgs with spikes. Draft message: "We're seeing high error rates due to a traffic surge tied to your API key. We've put temporary limits in place to protect platform stability. Recommended action: upgrade SDK to v0.12.3 which includes improved retry/backoff defaults, or apply the provided backoff + idempotency patterns. We're monitoring and will follow up with timeline." Who should I send to for Acme? Maya/oli?

maya: Send to Acme on the existing pager contact and cc account exec. Use the draft. Oli, confirm metrics trending down and when we can relax limits.

oli: Metrics after mitigation: error rate dropped from 8% -> 1.4% in ~40s, p95 latency down to 760ms. We'll keep rate limit and streaming disabled for 20m stabilization window, then reevaluate.

jordan: I'll cut an emergency SDK patch (rc) with the new defaults and a one-line migration note. Release artifact: sdk-js@0.12.3-rc.1. Pushing changelog and a short snippet for customers to set Idempotency-Key header.

maya: Thanks. I'll update the incident doc https://redwood/incident/INC-2026-17 with mitigation steps and link to the SDK advisory. Handoff to oli for continued monitoring for the next hour. Jordan, please publish the advisory and ping #customers once rc is stable. Sam please send the customer note now (short + actionable).

oli: Oncall takeover acknowledged. I'll keep watch and will re-enable streaming for the key only after a safe ramp. If anything regresses, escalate back to page. :thumbsup: 

sre-bot: NOTE - mitigation window started by oli at 1769954345, monitoring alerts suppressed for 15m.

maya: Creating a follow-up ticket for RCA and long-term mitigations: INC-2026-17-RCA. Include ideas: per-key burst allowances, client-side best-practice docs, and automated SDK quick-patch rollout mechanism for emergency defaults.

sam: Sent Acme note and opened support ticket SUP-4821. Will update thread with any replies.

jordan: Published rc and added the backoff snippet to the SDK repo with a short blog post. Link: https://redwood.dev/sdk/retry-guidance

maya: Closing the paging loop from my side — handing ongoing monitoring to oli. Thanks everyone for the quick coordination.

oli: Copy — will follow up with final metrics and confirm when we remove the temporary limits.
